.TH KNOBU 1 "November 2026" "knobu 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
knobu \- PowerToys-style utilities for Ubuntu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B knobu
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Knobu adds small power tools to the desktop: touchpad gestures for volume and
media, key and shortcut remapping, keeping the computer awake, a colour picker,
a text extractor, a clipboard history manager, a command bar quick launcher, and mouse & keyboard utilities (snippets, quit protection, debouncing, and independent wheel scrolling). Without a command, it opens the settings app.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B settings
Open the settings app (the default).
.TP
.B command-bar
Open the Command Bar quick launcher (alias: \fBrun\fR).
.TP
.B clipboard
Open the Clipboard History floating palette.
.TP
.B cleaning-mode
Launch the fullscreen Hardware Cleaning Mode overlay that locks inputs safely.
.TP
.B screen-ruler
Measure pixel distances and bounding boxes on screen.
.TP
.B find-mouse
Spotlight cursor location on screen.
.TP
.B notifications
Open the Mac-style Notification Center drawer.
.TP
.B ports
Print listening TCP/UDP ports and processes.
.TP
.BR backup " [path]"
Export all Knobu configurations to a JSON backup file.
.TP
.BR restore " path"
Restore Knobu configurations from a JSON backup file.
.TP
.B mic-mute
Toggle global default microphone mute.
.TP
.B audio-switch
Cycle default audio output device between speakers and headphones.
.TP
.B streams
List active application audio playback streams and volumes.
.TP
.B always-on-top
Pin or unpin the active window above all other windows.
.TP
.B fancyzones
Open the interactive FancyZones layout editor overlay.
.TP
.BR snap " zone"
Snap the active window to a FancyZones zone index (0, 1, 2...).
.TP
.B sysmon
Display live CPU, RAM, thermal, and network metrics.
.TP
.BR cidr " subnet"
Calculate IPv4/IPv6 CIDR network range, netmask, and usable hosts.
.TP
.BR dns " domain"
Query DNS records (A, AAAA, CNAME, MX, TXT) with custom resolver support.
.TP
.BR ssl-check " host:port"
Inspect SSL/TLS certificate expiration days, issuer, and SANs.
.TP
.B aws-whoami
Display active AWS caller identity (Account ID, ARN, UserId).
.TP
.B containers
List Docker containers status and exposed ports.
.TP
.B cron
Show local cron service status and list user cron jobs.
.TP
.BR cron-add " <expression> <command>"
Add a new user cron job with validation.
.TP
.B automations
List configured rule-based automations.
.TP
.BR run-automation " id"
Manually run an automation rule by ID or name.
.TP
.B shortcut-guide
Open the interactive Shortcut Guide overlay.
.TP
.B zoomit
Freeze screen for zoom & pen/arrow/box annotation.
.TP
.B quick-accent
Open the Quick Accent character picker popup.
.TP
.BR theme " [dark|light|toggle]"
Switch or inspect desktop light/dark theme.
.TP
.BR workspace " [name]"
Launch a saved workspace app group or list groups.
.TP
.B enable
Start the background service now and at every login.
.TP
.B disable
Stop the background service and remove it from login.
.TP
.B status
Show whether the background service is running.
.TP
.BR awake " on|off|DURATION"
Keep the computer awake until turned off, or for a duration such as 30m or 1h30m.
.TP
.B pick-color
Pick a colour from the screen.
.TP
.B extract-text
Select an area of the screen and copy its text.
.TP
.BR bypass " [on|off|toggle|status]"
Temporarily bypass all hardware grabs and customizations (useful for gaming and VMs).
.TP
.B restore-os-shortcuts
Restore default OS desktop shortcuts overridden by Knobu.
.TP
.B daemon
Run the background service in the foreground, for debugging.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/knobu/config.toml
Settings.
.SH NOTES
Reading touchpads and keyboards requires membership of the \fBinput\fR group.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/Aries-Surya/knobu
